.TH TEXT_KILLER 1 "2026-11-20" "text_killer @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
text_killer \- terminal text editor with an IRC-style interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B text_killer
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B text_killer \-\-cat
.I FILE
.br
.B text_killer \-\-convert
.I INPUT OUTPUT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B text_killer
is a full-screen terminal text editor whose look is modelled on IRC clients:
open documents are listed on the left like channels, with a topic bar,
status bar and a command line at the bottom.
.PP
Documents are shown in one continuous column by default. A page view lays
them out as US Letter pages (65 columns by 54 lines) side by side, as many
as fit the window, at actual size or stretched to
fill it. The original continuous
view, page sizes, themes and other options are in the options menu
(F2 or Ctrl+P); they can be remembered across sessions under
Options \(-> Settings.
.PP
It highlights 93 programming and markup languages, opens office documents
and e-books (.odt, .ods, .odp, .docx, .xlsx, .pptx, .rtf, .epub, .gz) as
editable text, and saves .odt, .docx and .rtf with headings, lists, bold,
italic and page breaks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-cat " FILE"
Print FILE as text (documents are converted) and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-convert " INPUT OUTPUT"
Convert INPUT to OUTPUT; the format comes from OUTPUT's extension.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
F1 help, F2 or Ctrl+P menu, Ctrl+O open, Ctrl+S save, F12 save as,
Ctrl+W close, Ctrl+Q quit, Ctrl+F find, Ctrl+R replace, Ctrl+G go to line,
Alt+Enter page break, Alt+1..9 switch window.
See the manual for the complete list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/text_killer/settings.conf
Remembered settings (Linux; %APPDATA%\\text_killer on Windows,
~/Library/Application Support/text_killer on macOS). Created only when
"Remember" is turned on.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TEXT_KILLER_CONFIG
Use this settings file instead of the default location.
